# ============================================================================
# ALLOWLIST .gitignore — deny everything, then admit the audio estate.
#
# This repository is rooted at the CLAUDE folder, which is a 2.9 GB working
# directory holding video, photography, scripts, HAR captures and a decade of
# unrelated work. The audio estate inside it is about 5 MB. A denylist would
# be a list of every mistake somebody thought of in advance; this is the other
# way round, and the only files git can see are the ones named below.
#
# TWO THINGS IN THIS FOLDER MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED, and the leading `*` is
# what guarantees it rather than the explicit rules further down:
#   - www.patreon.com*.har — browser captures containing session_id,
#     authorization and cookie values. A live login in plaintext.
#   - the video and image files, which are hundreds of megabytes each.
#
# Verify, do not trust. After any edit here:
#     git status --porcelain            # must list ONLY estate paths
#     git check-ignore -v www.patreon.com.har
#     du -sh $(git ls-files | head -1000)
# ============================================================================

# --- deny everything, including directory contents -------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# --- admit the estate ------------------------------------------------------
!/shared/
!/AUTOPSY/
!/RIGOR/
!/CASKET/

# --- admit the estate's tooling --------------------------------------------
# tools/counts.js derives every live number in the docs from the gates that
# produce them; tools/counts.json is its cache and must be tracked, or CI
# would re-run the slow harnesses on every push.
!/tools/

# --- admit the estate's documents, by exact name ---------------------------
!/AUDIO_INTERCHANGE.md
!/AUTOPSY_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/RIGOR_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/CASKET_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/LICENSE
!/README.md

# --- admit ONLY the estate's workflows -------------------------------------
# NECROPHONE's build.yml also lives in .github/workflows but its sources are
# scattered across the CLAUDE root and NECROPHONE-repo/, neither of which is
# in this repository. Committing it would add a job that could only ever fail.
!/.github/
/.github/*
!/.github/workflows/
/.github/workflows/*
!/.github/workflows/casket.yml
!/.github/workflows/autopsy.yml
!/.github/workflows/rigor.yml

# ============================================================================
# Now the ordinary exclusions, applied INSIDE the admitted directories.
# ============================================================================

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
build/
cmake-build-*/
*.o
*.a
*.dylib
*.so
*.dll
*.exe
*_artefacts/
JUCE/
node_modules/

# --- compiled parity gates (the source is tracked, the binaries are not) ---
core_parity
casket_parity
casket_parity_lto
cp0
cp2
cp3

# --- harness scratch -------------------------------------------------------
# RIGOR's mutation harness writes these while it runs. Committing one would
# capture a deliberately broken core as though it were the real thing.
*.__mut.js
*.__probe.js
.__mut_test.js
*.tailmark
__wtest.txt

# --- rendered audio --------------------------------------------------------
# Renders are outputs of the suite, reproducible from the code that made them.
*.wav
*.aiff
*.aif
*.flac
*.mp3

# --- OS and editor ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
.~lock.*#

# The Underworld charter (Masterbox↔trilogy boundary law) — admitted to the allowlist
!/UNDERWORLD_CHARTER.md
# ...and its engineering annex (preset schema, build boundary, module collision).
# The charter states the law; this one states the mechanics. Both or neither.
!/UNDERWORLD_INTERCHANGE.md
# The Underworld's own code (the consumer side): spike + translator + diagnostics.
!/underworld/
